        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage3Constant For each draw mode, the left quad is drawn twice (so that every vertex output buffer is covered) with a shader that writes oT3 = (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0) for every vertex. The right quad is then drawn with a shader that does not write oT3. Texture stage 3 is in PASS_THROUGH mode and the combiner outputs TEX3, so each quad shows its texture coordinate as a color. The right quad matches the left if oT3 carries over from the previous draw.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage3Reprime For each draw mode, the left quad is drawn twice with oT3 = (1.0, 0.25, 0.0, 1.0), the middle quad twice with oT3 = (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0), then the right quad is drawn with a shader that does not write oT3. Each quad shows its texture coordinate as a color. The right quad matches the middle quad if oT3 carries over from the most recent draw.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage3PerVertex For each draw mode, draws 12 points on the top row with oT3 taken from a per-vertex attribute (12 distinct colors), then 12 points in the same columns on the bottom row with a shader that does not write oT3. Each point shows its texture coordinate as a color, so the color of a bottom point identifies the primed vertex it inherited from, if any (e.g., the six vertex round robin pattern observed for fog in <ref refid="d1/d48/classFogCarryoverTests" kindref="compound">FogCarryoverTests</ref>).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage0Constant As Stage3Constant, for oT0 using texture stage 0.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage0Reprime As Stage3Reprime, for oT0 using texture stage 0.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>Stage0PerVertex As Stage3PerVertex, for oT0 using texture stage 0. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
